# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Why this file exists: HelpUI generates web projects by copying the packaged
# templates and static assets, and its golden tests assert those copies are
# **byte-for-byte identical** to the packaged source. With git's default
# `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows, a fresh clone would rewrite the templates to
# CRLF while the generator writes LF, so the golden comparison would fail on a
# clean checkout even though the working tree looked fine locally.
#
# Forcing LF in the repository (and telling git not to convert on checkout)
# makes generation reproducible across platforms: same input -> same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.zstd binary
*.db binary

# Minified third-party asset: vendored verbatim, not ours to reformat.
helpui/static/htmx.min.js -text
